;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "STAGEZ-07 -- the readers that DO work, pinned on their invariants")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;==== STAGEZ-07 -- the readers that DO work, pinned on their invariants · 01 · namespace ==== ====
(print "--- [STAGEZ-07 -- the readers that DO work, pinned on their invariants · 01 · namespace] ---")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [STAGEZ-07 . 01 . constants and branch words] ---")
;;Most of DPL-UR's 63 unreached functions are not blocked by anything -- no ids, no admin gate, no
;;missing fixture. Nothing had simply ever called them. These are those, and they are asserted on
;;INVARIANTS rather than on "it returned something", because a UI reads the exact values.
(map print
    [
        ;;these two feed key construction across the whole module; a change breaks every derived key
        (expect "<<STAGEZ-07>> the namespace constant DPL-UR builds keys from"
            "ouronet-ns" (DPL-UR.CT_Namespace))
        (expect "<<STAGEZ-07>> ...and the field separator, likewise"
            "|" (DPL-UR.CT_Bar))
        ;;all three branches of the pool-type word, so the mapping cannot be silently re-lettered
        (expect "<<STAGEZ-07>> S pools read as Stable"    ["S" "Stable"]   (O-UI-TWELVE.URC_PoolTypeWord "S|A|B"))
        (expect "<<STAGEZ-07>> P pools read as Product"   ["P" "Product"]  (O-UI-TWELVE.URC_PoolTypeWord "P|A|B"))
        ;;NOTE the spelling. "Weigthed" is a TYPO in the source, and it is user-visible. It is pinned
        ;;as-is deliberately: this test records the current UI string, it does not bless it. Fixing
        ;;the typo SHOULD fail here, at which point update the expectation in the same commit.
        (expect "<<STAGEZ-07>> W pools read as Weigthed [sic -- typo pinned as-behaves]"
            ["W" "Weigthed"] (O-UI-TWELVE.URC_PoolTypeWord "W|A|B|C"))
    ]
)
(commit-tx)

;;|| NEXT >
;;
(begin-tx "STAGEZ-08 -- the STOA collection split, pinned on CONSERVATION")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;==== STAGEZ-08 -- the STOA collection split, pinned on CONSERVATION · 01 · namespace ==== =======
(print "--- [STAGEZ-08 -- the STOA collection split, pinned on CONSERVATION · 01 · namespace] ---")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
(print "--- [STAGEZ-08 . 01 . four receivers, and no dust] ---")
;;A STOA payment is divided 10/20/30/40 between four protocol accounts. The failure that matters
;;for a money-splitter is not "wrong shape", it is VALUE LEAKING: parts that no longer sum to the
;;input because each was rounded down independently. So that is what is asserted, across a spread
;;of prices chosen to break it -- a round number, a price that does not divide evenly, and two
;;BELOW the 12-dp STOA precision where naive truncation would round a share to zero and silently
;;keep the remainder.
;;
;;RETARGETED 2026-09-25, AND THE RETARGET IS AN IMPROVEMENT. This used to call
;;DPL-UR::URC_SplitStoaPriceForReceivers, a display wrapper that zipped the shares onto the
;;receiver list. Archive mode deleted it -- zero callers anywhere -- and for a moment that read
;;as a reason to KEEP the wrapper, which inverts the dependency: a test exists to pin behaviour,
;;not to pin code in place. The behaviour lives in U|DALOS::UC_TenTwentyThirtyFourtySplit, and
;;asserting it there reaches the arithmetic instead of a caller of it.
(map print
    [
        (expect "<<STAGEZ-08>> the split conserves value exactly at every price, sub-precision included"
            [true true true true true true]
            (map (lambda (p:decimal)
                     (= p (fold (+) 0.0
                              (U|DALOS.UC_TenTwentyThirtyFourtySplit p (U|CT.CT_STOA_PRECISION)))))
                 [100.0 33.33 0.07 1.0 0.000000000001 0.123456789012345]))
        ;;and the proportions really are 10/20/30/40, not merely a partition that happens to sum
        (expect "<<STAGEZ-08>> ...in exactly 10/20/30/40 proportion"
            [10.0 20.0 30.0 40.0]
            (U|DALOS.UC_TenTwentyThirtyFourtySplit 100.0 (U|CT.CT_STOA_PRECISION)))
        ;;the four receivers must be DISTINCT: a collision would silently pay one account twice
        ;;and another nothing, while every sum-based check above still passed. Read straight from
        ;;DALOS now -- the wrapper that used to assemble this list is gone.
        (expect "<<STAGEZ-08>> the four receivers are distinct -- a collision double-pays one account"
            4
            (length (distinct
                [(DALOS.UR_AccountStoa (at 2 (DALOS.UR_DemiurgoiID)))
                 (DALOS.UR_AccountStoa (DALOS.GOV|DALOS|SC_NAME))
                 (DALOS.UR_AccountStoa (at 1 (DALOS.UR_DemiurgoiID)))
                 (DALOS.UR_AccountStoa (DALOS.GOV|OUROBOROS|SC_NAME))])))
    ]
)
(commit-tx)

